From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:19:34 +0800
Subject: web/tab-position: switching tabs keeps each session's place

Coming back to a session's tab opened it at the bottom: upstream pins the bottom whenever the
session changes, the saved place was restored only once per page load, and the next save then
forgot it. Leaving a session now saves its place (and whether it was following) while its rows
are still on screen, and opening it again restores that place; one left at the bottom stays
there. The bottom pin on a session change waits for the restore, as the hash scroll already did.

The restore runs before the next paint: placed, then corrected once against real layout (the
first estimate missed by the header height), so the first frame of the returning session already
shows the place instead of the bottom and then a jump. It waits for the returning view to
register (restoring with the previous session's view failed).

Ocelot-Patch: web/tab-position

